stage: 2
finding: Two claim failures. `src/project/vite-command.ts` uses `bun x vite`, which does not require the project's Vite: in an empty temp directory with no local Vite, `bun x vite --version` silently resolved/downloaded 80 packages and ran Vite 8.3.1. The delegation integration fixture symlinks Shallot's `node_modules`, so it cannot catch this fallback. Also, `startViteDev` truncates the reported URL to the origin/root and only matches loopback hosts. With Vite `base: "/game/"`, `--host 0.0.0.0`, and `--port 41989`, Vite reported `http://localhost:41989/game/` but Shallot passed `http://localhost:41989/`; the custom port survived. Binding `--host 192.168.0.139` made Vite report only a Network URL, which the regex rejects, leaving `startViteDev` waiting forever. Thus native dev does not reliably load the project's actual Vite URL.
